1
00:00:01,208 --> 00:00:02,000
[dramatic music]

2
00:00:04,167 --> 00:00:08,833
Ha! This isn't real, right?
This is a prank!

3
00:00:11,333 --> 00:00:16,083
[Nya] I'm sorry, but
I really don't think--

4
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:17,625
The dragon masters
are too powerful

5
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:19,833
to have been turned to stone.

6
00:00:17,625 --> 00:00:21,208
I pulled this once.
Remember, Kai?

7
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:24,917
Wyldfyre

8
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:23,667
Time to wake them
from their slumber.

9
00:00:24,917 --> 00:00:30,167
Ooh!
I'm gonna

10
00:00:27,292 --> 00:00:28,708
Goochee-goochee-goo!
[laughs]

11
00:00:30,167 --> 00:00:33,167
Egalt totally hates this,
don'tcha?

12
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,333
Goocheegoocheegooo?

13
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:41,167
Okay, plan B.

14
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:42,375
Ow!

15
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:45,042
All right.

16
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:47,833
Stone. Bad idea.

17
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:50,042
[sighs] Okay, so
it's not a prank,

18
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:51,833
but it'll wear off, right?

19
00:00:50,042 --> 00:00:55,000
Right?

20
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:58,708
-I'm not sure.
-Lloyd?

21
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,042
I don't know. And we don't
have time to find out.

22
00:00:58,708 --> 00:01:01,917
The Blood Moon's already rising,

23
00:01:00,042 --> 00:01:03,833
which means Ras
can start the ritual

24
00:01:01,917 --> 00:01:06,292
to free the Forbidden Five,

25
00:01:03,833 --> 00:01:07,750
which will unleash evil on our
world like we've never known.

26
00:01:06,292 --> 00:01:11,208
[Arin] But-- but that'll
never happen.

27
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:12,542
Kai, you've mastered
Rising Dragon technique.

28
00:01:11,208 --> 00:01:13,750
All we gotta do is--

29
00:01:12,542 --> 00:01:15,500
I haven't mastered
Rising Dragon.

30
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:18,917
Look, I did it once.

31
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:20,375
We could practice it more.
Then you could teach us.

32
00:01:18,917 --> 00:01:22,708
But that's just it.

33
00:01:20,375 --> 00:01:26,000
I don't know how I did it.
Not exactly.

34
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:28,375
It's the only fighting style
that can defeat Shatterspin.

35
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,083
Is there any other way
to stop Ras's ritual?

36
00:01:28,375 --> 00:01:35,375
There's gotta be something.

37
00:01:30,083 --> 00:01:32,500
No, not now! I can't handle
more visions! [yells]

38
00:01:35,375 --> 00:01:36,375
[Cole] The Wyldness!

39
00:01:38,042 --> 00:01:39,458
-Help! Help!
-[ominous music]

40
00:01:43,042 --> 00:01:46,750
[gong rings]

41
00:01:45,458 --> 00:01:48,500
[Lloyd gasping]

42
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:51,792
Lloyd! Are you okay?

43
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:54,083
More visions. I still can't
control when they come.

44
00:01:51,792 --> 00:01:57,375
But I think I know
where we have to go.

45
00:01:54,083 --> 00:02:00,625
Ras is going to perform
his ritual in the Wyldness.

46
00:01:57,375 --> 00:01:59,750
We may not be ready,
but we don't have a choice.

47
00:02:00,625 --> 00:02:04,792
It's time to face Ras,
or everything will be lost.

48
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:13,208
<i>♪ Lost in the unknown,</i>
<i>so much to see ♪</i>

49
00:02:10,208 --> 00:02:16,500
<i>♪ Together we will rise ♪</i>

50
00:02:13,208 --> 00:02:13,875
<i>♪ We fight ♪</i>

51
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,125
<i>♪ Be a Ninja for what's right ♪</i>

52
00:02:21,125 --> 00:02:23,000
-[explosion booming]
-[dramatic music]

53
00:02:24,458 --> 00:02:27,292
[guns blasting]

54
00:02:31,292 --> 00:02:32,417
Get him!

55
00:02:33,708 --> 00:02:37,083
File this permit in triplicate!

56
00:02:43,208 --> 00:02:49,875
Really?

57
00:02:45,083 --> 00:02:48,208
What? There aren't that many
places I can use that joke.

58
00:02:49,875 --> 00:02:53,417
Focus on deactivating
the equipment known as Zane.

59
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:59,667
That is really quite rude.
Could equipment do this?

60
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:06,417
[shurikens clanking]

61
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:05,500
I mean, depending on its
programming, but point taken.

62
00:03:06,417 --> 00:03:09,917
[guns blasting]

63
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,792
Ya!

64
00:03:18,292 --> 00:03:23,625
Ha, and that old biddy Janet

65
00:03:20,583 --> 00:03:24,792
said my crystal ball
didn't work right.

66
00:03:23,625 --> 00:03:26,042
[crystal ball zapping]

67
00:03:24,792 --> 00:03:31,250
[body thudding]

68
00:03:26,042 --> 00:03:28,375
What does she know?
Works great.

69
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:32,375
[crystal ball beeping]

70
00:03:35,417 --> 00:03:41,167
-Well, mostly.
-[whimsical music]

71
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:42,750
-[gas whizzes]
-Oh, ah! The onion!

72
00:03:41,167 --> 00:03:45,000
Oh, my eyes are watering!

73
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:46,833
Oh, the stench burns!
Oh, it burns!

74
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:45,750
[guns blasting]

75
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:50,208
[crystal ball zapping]

76
00:03:53,500 --> 00:04:00,292
[dramatic music]

77
00:03:55,792 --> 00:03:57,125
Come at me!

78
00:04:00,292 --> 00:04:01,625
I did ask for that.

79
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:09,958
Surrender the equipment now,

80
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:13,833
or we will charge you
with an additional violation.

81
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:16,625
Statute 27a, subparagraph 9.

82
00:04:13,833 --> 00:04:19,542
That statute is just a fine.

83
00:04:16,625 --> 00:04:20,958
You've already ordered
all of us terminated.

84
00:04:19,542 --> 00:04:22,042
Right. Fair point.

85
00:04:20,958 --> 00:04:23,417
Guess fines aren't
really an issue

86
00:04:22,042 --> 00:04:24,625
if you're no longer alive.

87
00:04:23,417 --> 00:04:25,792
My bad.

88
00:04:24,625 --> 00:04:27,458
[metal clanking]

89
00:04:25,792 --> 00:04:29,333
[guns blasting]

90
00:04:27,458 --> 00:04:31,750
[crystal ball chimes]

91
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:33,875
[coconuts thudding]

92
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:35,542
Wow, coconuts. That's a first.

93
00:04:33,875 --> 00:04:38,792
[guns blasting]

94
00:04:35,542 --> 00:04:41,292
Come on! We've got to keep
them away from Bonzle!

95
00:04:38,792 --> 00:04:42,875
[crystal ball zapping]

96
00:04:41,292 --> 00:04:46,208
I said,

97
00:04:42,875 --> 00:04:48,583
by the all-encompassing
authority of the Administration,

98
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:52,083
I hereby demand your surrender.

99
00:04:48,583 --> 00:04:51,083
Um no

100
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:55,292
thank you.

101
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:57,750
[sighs] You're an accomplice

102
00:04:55,292 --> 00:05:00,917
of the equipment
called Zane, right?

103
00:04:57,750 --> 00:05:03,583
Rules say I have
to put you under arrest.

104
00:05:00,917 --> 00:05:06,792
You could put me
under arrest, sure,

105
00:05:03,583 --> 00:05:06,042
but I get the sense your
heart's not really in it.

106
00:05:06,792 --> 00:05:09,542
Yeah, you're probably right.
Seems a little silly to me.

107
00:05:11,625 --> 00:05:16,583
Ah, this job is really
rulesy, you know?

108
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:18,375
I don't remember
what I used to do

109
00:05:16,583 --> 00:05:21,667
before the Administration,

110
00:05:18,375 --> 00:05:24,042
but this is not the coolest
career or anything. [chuckles]

111
00:05:21,667 --> 00:05:26,042
Oh, well, I'm supposed
to capture you,

112
00:05:24,042 --> 00:05:28,917
so can you just let me do that?

113
00:05:26,042 --> 00:05:30,208
Don't make it weird, hmm?

114
00:05:28,917 --> 00:05:35,708
[dramatic music]

115
00:05:30,208 --> 00:05:33,167
Hey! Get outta here, nightlight!

116
00:05:35,708 --> 00:05:39,875
Ah! Knock it off!

117
00:05:37,792 --> 00:05:42,292
[bright music]

118
00:05:39,875 --> 00:05:40,292
What the

119
00:05:42,292 --> 00:05:48,708
-Whoa!
-[electricity crackling]

120
00:05:47,042 --> 00:05:51,167
How did you know I can do that?

121
00:05:48,708 --> 00:05:52,708
No one knows I can
control lightning,

122
00:05:51,167 --> 00:05:54,292
and no one can find out.

123
00:05:52,708 --> 00:05:57,375
[dramatic music]

124
00:05:54,292 --> 00:06:00,500
Ah!

125
00:05:57,375 --> 00:06:03,750
Get away! You're
making this so weird!

126
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:06,000
[Jiro roars]

127
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:07,250
We'll get you in
a minute, buddy.

128
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:12,083
-[dramatic music]
-[metal thudding]

129
00:06:07,250 --> 00:06:10,000
This is so easy.
It almost seems unfair.

130
00:06:12,083 --> 00:06:13,875
[buttons beeping]

131
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:22,708
I quipped too soon.

132
00:06:18,417 --> 00:06:24,875
[dramatic music continues]

133
00:06:22,708 --> 00:06:28,667
[ice crackling]

134
00:06:24,875 --> 00:06:26,625
That's one down!

135
00:06:28,667 --> 00:06:33,625
[metal thuds]

136
00:06:30,708 --> 00:06:36,083
[sword clanks]

137
00:06:33,625 --> 00:06:35,000
That's two!

138
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:39,667
[crystal ball zapping]

139
00:06:42,250 --> 00:06:48,208
Three, four, five!

140
00:06:46,083 --> 00:06:46,875
I'm crushing it!

141
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:50,625
[dramatic music continues]

142
00:06:53,667 --> 00:06:57,542
Are you properly
licensed to drive?

143
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:04,292
-[ice crunches]
-[dramatic music continues]

144
00:07:02,333 --> 00:07:06,500
[guns blasting]

145
00:07:04,292 --> 00:07:09,958
Keep them away while I
hack into their system.

146
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,542
Wouldn't kill you
to say please, but sure.

147
00:07:09,958 --> 00:07:13,542
[crystal ball zapping]

148
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:19,042
I just need a bit more time

149
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:19,167
so I can set them
all to self-destruct.

150
00:07:19,042 --> 00:07:20,750
[Cole] You got it!

151
00:07:29,417 --> 00:07:31,083
Connecting to the system.

152
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:35,000
[guns blasting]

153
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:41,000
-[metal clanks]
-[electricity crackling]

154
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:43,458
[Zane] Data breach is failing!

155
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,042
Can't connect! Error!

156
00:07:43,458 --> 00:07:45,833
Powering down.

157
00:07:53,625 --> 00:07:59,458
Zane.

158
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:57,958
[dramatic music]

159
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:05,167
Zane! [grunts]

160
00:08:01,708 --> 00:08:03,125
Talk to me, buddy.

161
00:08:05,167 --> 00:08:07,958
[metal clanks]

162
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:14,708
[Cole shouts]

163
00:08:12,667 --> 00:08:15,875
Are you okay in there?

164
00:08:14,708 --> 00:08:18,125
[gun blasts]

165
00:08:15,875 --> 00:08:20,708
I think his circuits got fried.

166
00:08:18,125 --> 00:08:22,167
He just needs a little reboot.

167
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:23,917
What's the magic word?

168
00:08:22,167 --> 00:08:25,333
Uh
Please?

169
00:08:23,917 --> 00:08:29,917
Finally!

170
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:28,917
[crystal ball zapping]

171
00:08:29,917 --> 00:08:34,417
[mech whirring]

172
00:08:32,292 --> 00:08:38,000
-Huh?
-Zane! Are you okay?

173
00:08:34,417 --> 00:08:40,167
[Zane] Confirmed.
All systems are stabilized.

174
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:42,167
And decoding is reactivating.

175
00:08:40,167 --> 00:08:45,625
[computer beeping]

176
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:43,875
Data breach completed.
Hack attack!

177
00:08:45,625 --> 00:08:48,583
[metal clanking]

178
00:08:50,375 --> 00:08:53,208
[alert beeping]

179
00:08:56,875 --> 00:09:01,667
Oh, this is gonna
be a lotta paperwork.

180
00:09:00,167 --> 00:09:05,042
[agents screaming]

181
00:09:01,667 --> 00:09:07,667
That can't be great.
[screams]

182
00:09:05,042 --> 00:09:10,000
[agent groaning]

183
00:09:07,667 --> 00:09:12,875
Hurry, no matter
how difficult it is,

184
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:14,833
we can't give up until
we find Bonzle, and--

185
00:09:12,875 --> 00:09:17,458
-I found you!
-I found her.

186
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:16,833
That went more smoothly
than anticipated.

187
00:09:17,458 --> 00:09:20,375
[dramatic music]

188
00:09:28,167 --> 00:09:31,917
The magical storehouse is near.

189
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,417
So what now?

190
00:09:31,917 --> 00:09:34,833
You're just gonna stuff
me in a storage box

191
00:09:33,417 --> 00:09:36,500
till the Blood Moon passes?

192
00:09:34,833 --> 00:09:38,750
Exactly.

193
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:41,583
Oh. I was kidding.

194
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:45,042
Magical Containment units
are incredibly safe.

195
00:09:41,583 --> 00:09:44,125
Small, but safe. You're not
claustrophobic, are you?

196
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:48,667
If so, this would be
a really bad time to find out.

197
00:09:54,042 --> 00:10:00,250
Oh, no. Look up ahead.

198
00:09:56,917 --> 00:09:59,292
[Cole] The Cloud Kingdom!
Are they following us?

199
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:01,583
Stay low!

200
00:10:06,875 --> 00:10:13,208
[foreboding music]

201
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:12,042
The magical storehouse
is just beyond these trees.

202
00:10:13,208 --> 00:10:16,875
[footsteps approaching]

203
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:22,792
Wolf Mask Warriors.

204
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,917
Could they know
where we're headed?

205
00:10:31,625 --> 00:10:33,292
[leaves rustling]

206
00:10:36,792 --> 00:10:39,542
This is not how I expected
my day to go, which is weird.

207
00:10:40,792 --> 00:10:47,083
I drink fortunetelling
tea every morning.

208
00:10:44,125 --> 00:10:50,708
You'd think it'd
give me a heads up.

209
00:10:47,083 --> 00:10:49,250
Jiro, stay hidden here.
We'll be right back.

210
00:10:50,708 --> 00:10:51,708
[Jiro growls]

211
00:10:55,583 --> 00:11:02,542
[ominous music]

212
00:10:58,667 --> 00:11:04,375
Lord Ras, I--
I've managed to find the Ninja.

213
00:11:02,542 --> 00:11:07,708
Not sure I can hold
the image for long.

214
00:11:04,375 --> 00:11:09,333
The Blood Moon is here,
and the Ninja are too close.

215
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:11,417
You have to stop them.

216
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:14,042
Uh, from here?

217
00:11:11,417 --> 00:11:17,708
That's impossible.
Can we send warriors?

218
00:11:14,042 --> 00:11:20,333
Use the forbidden magic
you've been studying, Jordana.

219
00:11:17,708 --> 00:11:22,792
But I'm a scientist.

220
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:24,417
I've only just started
learning the magic

221
00:11:22,792 --> 00:11:26,500
on the scrolls
you've shown me, and--

222
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:28,833
I have no tie for failure!

223
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:31,667
[Jordana sighs]

224
00:11:28,833 --> 00:11:30,667
The Ninja are far, but

225
00:11:31,667 --> 00:11:33,708
[Jordana groaning]

226
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,917
As far as I know,

227
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:41,375
the Wyldness should
be the land up ahead.

228
00:11:38,917 --> 00:11:40,875
-[thunder rumbling]
-[suspenseful music]

229
00:11:41,375 --> 00:11:44,167
Look out!
Hold on!

230
00:11:47,167 --> 00:11:49,042
Sora, watch out!

231
00:11:51,792 --> 00:11:54,333
This wind is unnatural.

232
00:11:59,250 --> 00:12:01,500
-Hold on!
-[all exclaiming]

233
00:12:03,208 --> 00:12:04,125
-[Arin grunts]
-No!

234
00:12:08,542 --> 00:12:10,542
[Lloyd screaming]

235
00:12:14,792 --> 00:12:16,833
This looks bad, this looks bad,
this looks bad!

236
00:12:20,333 --> 00:12:23,083
[everyone screaming]

237
00:12:21,917 --> 00:12:25,875
Worse than I thought!
Worse than I thought!

238
00:12:23,083 --> 00:12:24,125
Worse than I thought!

239
00:12:25,875 --> 00:12:29,000
[everyone screaming]

240
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:32,958
[foreboding music]

241
00:12:34,750 --> 00:12:40,667
-Are you kidding me?
-[ship creaking]

242
00:12:41,667 --> 00:12:45,708
[Sora and Kai gasping]

243
00:12:44,583 --> 00:12:46,833
Whee!

244
00:12:45,708 --> 00:12:50,958
Shh!

245
00:12:46,833 --> 00:12:49,625
No sudden movements.

246
00:12:50,958 --> 00:12:54,583
[both screaming]

247
00:12:52,917 --> 00:12:56,208
[both grunt]

248
00:12:54,583 --> 00:12:58,833
I can't believe it. We're safe.

249
00:12:56,208 --> 00:13:00,667
[both screaming]

250
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:02,667
Okay, now we're sa--

251
00:13:00,667 --> 00:13:05,083
[both screaming]

252
00:13:02,667 --> 00:13:06,458
-Now we're--
-[both screaming]

253
00:13:05,083 --> 00:13:11,083
Now we're--

254
00:13:06,458 --> 00:13:09,500
-[both screaming]
-[suspenseful music]

255
00:13:11,083 --> 00:13:14,708
[Lloyd screaming]

256
00:13:13,458 --> 00:13:16,792
You're flying!

257
00:13:14,708 --> 00:13:18,292
[Riyu growls]

258
00:13:16,792 --> 00:13:21,875
Or sort of flying.

259
00:13:18,292 --> 00:13:24,083
[screams]

260
00:13:21,875 --> 00:13:26,792
[Lloyd grunting]

261
00:13:24,083 --> 00:13:28,417
We're alive. You saved me!

262
00:13:26,792 --> 00:13:30,583
[Riyu growls]

263
00:13:28,417 --> 00:13:32,333
-[mysterious music]
-[ship creaking]

264
00:13:30,583 --> 00:13:33,750
Is everyone okay?

265
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:35,417
What's down there?

266
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:37,167
Oh, just nothingness.

267
00:13:35,417 --> 00:13:40,250
Instant doom.

268
00:13:37,167 --> 00:13:43,667
[foreboding music]

269
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:42,292
We need to get up to the top.

270
00:13:43,667 --> 00:13:46,458
My Climber Mech!

271
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:50,625
Day saved! Boom!

272
00:13:46,458 --> 00:13:49,292
[ship creaking]

273
00:13:50,625 --> 00:13:53,833
Please don't say boom.

274
00:13:52,417 --> 00:13:55,542
[chuckles] Oops!

275
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:58,542
[Sora] The Climber Mech
is a great idea,

276
00:13:55,542 --> 00:14:01,042
but we can't get to it
without tipping the ship.

277
00:13:58,542 --> 00:14:02,583
We'd for sure fall
into all that

278
00:14:01,042 --> 00:14:04,167
Ugh!

279
00:14:02,583 --> 00:14:06,750
[ominous music]

280
00:14:04,167 --> 00:14:10,958
Nothingness and instant doom.

281
00:14:06,750 --> 00:14:08,875
Yeah, that.

282
00:14:10,958 --> 00:14:16,292
If we jump together in
exactly the right place,

283
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:17,792
I think we can tilt the ship
enough in the right direction

284
00:14:16,292 --> 00:14:19,667
for Kai to get to the mech.

285
00:14:17,792 --> 00:14:22,917
I'm ready to try it.

286
00:14:19,667 --> 00:14:24,958
Okay, on the count of three,
we all jump,

287
00:14:22,917 --> 00:14:27,708
land hard, the ship tilts up.

288
00:14:24,958 --> 00:14:28,917
Then, Kai, you get to
the mech as fast as you can.

289
00:14:27,708 --> 00:14:30,417
-Got it?
-Got it!

290
00:14:28,917 --> 00:14:31,583
One.

291
00:14:30,417 --> 00:14:35,750
Two.

292
00:14:31,583 --> 00:14:37,250
-Three!
-[suspenseful music]

293
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:41,833
[Kai grunting]

294
00:14:37,250 --> 00:14:38,875
Piece of cake!

295
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:46,958
-Faster!
-Almost [screams]

296
00:14:44,167 --> 00:14:45,958
We're going over!

297
00:14:46,958 --> 00:14:51,833
[both screaming]

298
00:14:50,750 --> 00:14:54,250
Come on!

299
00:14:51,833 --> 00:14:52,708
Come on! Come on!

300
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:56,208
-[computer beeps]
-Yes!

301
00:15:00,708 --> 00:15:02,917
[both screaming]

302
00:15:07,792 --> 00:15:11,917
-[rocks thuds]
-[Kai sighs]

303
00:15:09,417 --> 00:15:13,500
-[rock thuds]
-[Kai yells]

304
00:15:11,917 --> 00:15:16,500
[pensive music]

305
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:18,125
Sorry,<i> Bounty.</i>
You were a real good ship.

306
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:19,708
But onward--

307
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:24,375
And upward.

308
00:15:19,708 --> 00:15:22,750
[Kai grunting]

309
00:15:24,375 --> 00:15:27,542
[mysterious music]

310
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:31,417
This is the magical
storage house?

311
00:15:32,750 --> 00:15:38,458
It's cute, but it doesn't
look big enough for all of us,

312
00:15:36,958 --> 00:15:43,667
or even one of us.

313
00:15:38,458 --> 00:15:41,292
-[whimsical music]
-You misunderstand magic.

314
00:15:43,667 --> 00:15:47,792
-[door rattling]
-Gah!

315
00:15:45,792 --> 00:15:50,875
Oh. It's stuck.

316
00:15:47,792 --> 00:15:52,208
[sorceress grunting]

317
00:15:50,875 --> 00:15:53,708
Ah!

318
00:15:52,208 --> 00:15:57,125
Hold this.

319
00:15:53,708 --> 00:15:59,417
Let me try an opening spell.

320
00:15:57,125 --> 00:16:00,750
And

321
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:04,375
[crystal ball zaps]

322
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:06,542
Ouch! Oh, for crying
out loud in the morning!

323
00:16:04,375 --> 00:16:07,917
-[footsteps approaching]
-Shh! Listen!

324
00:16:06,542 --> 00:16:07,542
They're almost here!

325
00:16:07,917 --> 00:16:11,542
[foreboding music]

326
00:16:15,375 --> 00:16:17,292
This should do it.

327
00:16:18,417 --> 00:16:21,917
[crystal ball zapping]

328
00:16:19,917 --> 00:16:23,250
[mysterious music]

329
00:16:21,917 --> 00:16:22,958
Ha! Take that, Janet!

330
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:25,417
Hurry! Let's go!

331
00:16:29,292 --> 00:16:32,750
[ominous music]

332
00:16:37,792 --> 00:16:40,000
[mysterious music]

333
00:16:46,167 --> 00:16:50,375
Okay.

334
00:16:47,875 --> 00:16:51,708
I do misunderstand magic.

335
00:16:50,375 --> 00:16:53,875
We did not anticipate

336
00:16:51,708 --> 00:16:58,500
the Wolf Mask Warriors
would be here.

337
00:16:53,875 --> 00:16:56,542
We must hide Bonzle quickly,
before we are discovered.

338
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:03,333
[whimsical music]

339
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:07,208
What is this place?

340
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:05,792
Hmm, this storage house
is where we mystical folks

341
00:17:07,208 --> 00:17:10,500
store most of our
valuable magical items.

342
00:17:12,167 --> 00:17:17,917
But nothing is alphabetized.

343
00:17:15,292 --> 00:17:19,583
This is highly inefficient.

344
00:17:17,917 --> 00:17:23,125
We have a system!

345
00:17:19,583 --> 00:17:20,792
Or we used to, probably.

346
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:25,625
Aha! There it is!

347
00:17:26,917 --> 00:17:32,667
Home, sweet
protective container.

348
00:17:29,792 --> 00:17:34,125
Is this bigger
on the inside, too?

349
00:17:32,667 --> 00:17:35,125
Yes.

350
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:36,833
Yeah.

351
00:17:35,125 --> 00:17:42,125
No. Sorry!

352
00:17:36,833 --> 00:17:38,167
Help me get this out.

353
00:17:42,125 --> 00:17:44,625
That looked expensive.

354
00:17:43,375 --> 00:17:50,042
And cursed.

355
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:47,917
But we have more
pressing concerns here.

356
00:17:50,042 --> 00:17:55,708
This is my second-most
powerful creation.

357
00:17:53,833 --> 00:17:58,125
After you, of course, my dear.

358
00:17:55,708 --> 00:18:01,417
You will be perfectly
safe in here.

359
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:04,917
Once I have sealed it, no
one will be able to open it.

360
00:18:01,417 --> 00:18:07,667
Not even this Lord Ras
you keep telling me about.

361
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:09,958
Do I really have to?

362
00:18:07,667 --> 00:18:11,958
Just until
the Blood Moon passes,

363
00:18:09,958 --> 00:18:14,750
which hopefully
won't be much longer.

364
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:18,250
Ras's army is hunting for us.

365
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:21,208
I regret, we have no
other options, Bonzle.

366
00:18:18,250 --> 00:18:23,625
You'll be fine, dear.

367
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:26,250
Okay.

368
00:18:23,625 --> 00:18:29,792
Oh, this is actually kinda cozy.

369
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:31,000
I'm going to seal you in
now and start the spell.

370
00:18:29,792 --> 00:18:33,250
You ready?

371
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:36,292
[sighs] As ready
as I'll ever be.

372
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:38,875
I do not believe in
wishing people good luck,

373
00:18:36,292 --> 00:18:41,667
but I hope random
probability outcomes

374
00:18:38,875 --> 00:18:40,625
align to your benefit.

375
00:18:41,667 --> 00:18:45,625
[clears throat]

376
00:18:44,083 --> 00:18:47,208
[speaking in foreign language]

377
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:48,958
[clears throat] Nope.

378
00:18:47,208 --> 00:18:50,375
[speaking in foreign language]

379
00:18:48,958 --> 00:18:52,875
Can you not look
at me for a sec?

380
00:18:50,375 --> 00:18:55,000
I get nervous under pressure.

381
00:18:52,875 --> 00:18:53,667
[Zane whistling]

382
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
[speaking in foreign language]

383
00:19:09,958 --> 00:19:11,875
Wow. She really knows
what she's doing.

384
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,958
[speaking in foreign language]

385
00:19:17,542 --> 00:19:20,875
Whoa!

386
00:19:19,750 --> 00:19:22,083
Wait, no.

387
00:19:20,875 --> 00:19:24,125
What, no?

388
00:19:22,083 --> 00:19:26,750
I'm not doing that.

389
00:19:24,125 --> 00:19:30,833
-Then who is?
-I don't know!

390
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:29,333
What's happening?
Let me out, let me out!

391
00:19:30,833 --> 00:19:36,167
Get her out of there!

392
00:19:31,833 --> 00:19:34,208
I'm trying!

393
00:19:36,167 --> 00:19:41,667
[Zane] Look!
The runes are appearing.

394
00:19:38,583 --> 00:19:44,167
It is Theroxian,
the forbidden language.

395
00:19:41,667 --> 00:19:42,958
Come on!

396
00:19:44,167 --> 00:19:45,625
[grunts] What the

397
00:19:48,208 --> 00:19:50,250
-[Bonzle yells]
-[Kai gasps]

398
00:19:52,542 --> 00:19:56,833
Thank you, Ninja.

399
00:19:54,458 --> 00:19:58,583
Who are you?
What have you done?

400
00:19:56,833 --> 00:20:01,625
Never seen her
before in my life.

401
00:19:58,583 --> 00:20:04,458
[yells] My name is Jordana!

402
00:20:01,625 --> 00:20:06,208
Oh, you Ninja, especially
the one you call Sora,

403
00:20:04,458 --> 00:20:07,500
are my sworn enemies.

404
00:20:06,208 --> 00:20:09,125
Still not ringing a bell.

405
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:12,792
[yells]

406
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:11,583
I knew I could trap you
with my old Imperium tech,

407
00:20:12,792 --> 00:20:15,208
but I wasn't sure how I'd
contain the spell here.

408
00:20:16,833 --> 00:20:23,625
I never thought you'd put
her in a cage yourselves.

409
00:20:20,167 --> 00:20:26,208
I might be just learning
Theroxian magic,

410
00:20:23,625 --> 00:20:28,917
but corrupting your
poultry magic, sorceress,

411
00:20:26,208 --> 00:20:32,458
has proven to be quite simple.

412
00:20:28,917 --> 00:20:35,958
Lord Ras will be
very pleased with me.

413
00:20:32,458 --> 00:20:38,083
And now we have
everything we need

414
00:20:35,958 --> 00:20:40,750
to begin the ritual
of the Blood Moon.

415
00:20:38,083 --> 00:20:42,542
[Bonzle yelling]

416
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:45,750
Bonzle!

417
00:20:42,542 --> 00:20:48,542
You'll have plenty of time
to think about your failures

418
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:50,667
trapped in this stinky
old mushroom building.

419
00:20:48,542 --> 00:20:52,333
It's a mystical storehouse!

420
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:55,125
Don't care.

421
00:20:52,333 --> 00:20:58,583
We gotta get outta
here and save her!

422
00:20:55,125 --> 00:20:56,750
-[force field thuds]
-[Kai yells]

423
00:20:58,583 --> 00:21:03,250
-[suspenseful music]
-[both screaming]

424
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:05,125
[eerie music]

425
00:21:03,250 --> 00:21:08,583
[Lloyd grunts]

426
00:21:05,125 --> 00:21:10,833
Whoa. That storm
was so disorienting.

427
00:21:08,583 --> 00:21:12,542
I have no idea where we are,

428
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:12,583
or where the others
could've landed.

429
00:21:12,542 --> 00:21:16,500
Well, I'm thinking
we head toward that.

430
00:21:21,708 --> 00:21:24,417
[gentle music]

431
00:21:22,875 --> 00:21:26,958
[Riyu grunting]

432
00:21:24,417 --> 00:21:31,458
No, I don't know if
any of the other Ninja

433
00:21:26,958 --> 00:21:28,625
survived the fall, Riyu.

434
00:21:31,458 --> 00:21:38,000
But even if we're
the only two Ninja left,

435
00:21:34,833 --> 00:21:36,458
it's up to us to save the world.

436
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,125
[foreboding music]

437
00:21:44,917 --> 00:21:47,750
[closing theme music playing]

